KEY FINDING — RSS scales with PART COUNT (distinct #[cube] fns to expand +
monomorphize in one rustc process), NOT raw file count:
  p6 has the FEWEST files (4971) but the MOST parts (68) -> highest RSS (16.5 GB).
  p5 has the MOST files (9943) but only 14 parts -> 9.0 GB.
The file-count budget (10000) chosen as a conservative proxy still left ample
headroom; the canary-by-file-count was NOT actually the worst case, but every
shard (incl. the 68-part p6) compiled comfortably under 30 GB.

FACADE (load-bearing, key_risk 1): PASS at ~9.0 GB. Confirms verified_structural_fact 3
— the facade LINKS against the shards' already-expanded part fns and type-checks the
122 cross-crate #[cube] calls cheaply; it does NOT re-expand the part bodies. The
~9 GB is the facade's own 9 remaining output modules (exc/vxc/fxc/kxc unpol + pol,
lxc_unpol) being compiled in the same crate, not the lxc_pol parts.

